.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Routines for manipulating quadrants (neighbors, parents, children, etc\&.) 


.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int p8est_coordinates_compare (const \fBp4est_qcoord_t\fP v1[], const \fBp4est_qcoord_t\fP v2[])"

.PP
Compare two sets of coordinates in their Morton ordering\&. Coordinates are signed, but the sorted order will treat them as unsigned, with negative coordinates being greater than positive coordinates because of their representation in twos-complement\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIv1,v2\fP Two sets of 3d coordinates\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns < 0 if \fIv1\fP < \fIv2\fP, 0 if \fIv1\fP == \fIv2\fP, > 0 if \fIv1\fP > \fIv2\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int p8est_coordinates_is_inside_root (const \fBp4est_qcoord_t\fP coord[])"

.PP
Test if Morton indices are inside the unit tree or on its boundary\&. For this function, coordinate values of \fBP8EST_ROOT_LEN\fP are legal\&. It is like \fBp8est_quadrant_is_inside_root\fP with infinite level\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcoord\fP 3d coordinates\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true if \fI\fP(coord[0],coord[1],coord[2]) is inside the unit tree\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int p8est_coordinates_is_valid (const \fBp4est_qcoord_t\fP coord[], int level)"

.PP
